{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch14yh6UbLnmaiMBmCHRL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Length is not a mechanism to fix. The model **already** penalises length among distractors (within-question corr −0.27; −0.32 with overlap partialled out). Gold paragraphs are simply shorter than distractors in this data. Adding a stronger length penalty would be a dataset shortcut, so I'm dropping it.\n\nThe head readout is the more interesting lead:\n- **Question-reading heads:** in the last layer, 7 of 12 heads at [CLS] read the question tokens. This is the coverage read-out.\n- **Body-reading heads:** layer-5 heads 0 and 6 are the only heads that read the paragraph body (80–82% of their attention mass).\n\nBridge paragraphs contain the answer but cover only one hop of the question. So a natural causal hypothesis is that boosting the body-reading heads relative to the question-reading coverage heads lifts them.\n\nBefore spending a pass I'll prepare the per-head edit (scaling a head's 32 columns of `attention.output.dense`) and check head output norms. The title-direction output from the last block is still in flight and will inform the choice.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: (prep, no pass) per-head edit = scale the 32 input columns of layer-5 attention.output.dense belonging to a head; check sizes/norms.\nWao = load_original(\"bert.encoder.layer.5.attention.output.dense.weight\"); Wv5 = load_original(\"bert.encoder.layer.5.attention.self.value.weight\")\nprint(\"attn.output.dense\", tuple(Wao.shape), \"| value\", tuple(Wv5.shape))\nhn_ = [float(Wao[:, h*32:(h+1)*32].norm()) for h in range(12)]\nprint(\"L5 per-head output-column norms:\", np.round(hn_, 2))\n# weight-only alignment: how strongly can each head's output subspace write onto the readout axis r (via LN gamma)?\ngA5 = load_original(\"bert.encoder.layer.5.attention.output.LayerNorm.weight\").numpy()\nalign = [np.linalg.norm((Wao[:, h*32:(h+1)*32].numpy() * gA5[:, None]).T @ r_) / np.linalg.norm(Wao[:, h*32:(h+1)*32].numpy() * gA5[:, None]) for h in range(12)]\nprint(\"L5 per-head |proj of output subspace on r| / norm:\", np.round(align, 3))\ndef head_scale_edit(layer, scales):\n    \"\"\"scales: {head: factor}; multiplies the head's 32 columns of attention.output.dense.weight (bias untouched).\"\"\"\n    W = load_original(f\"bert.encoder.layer.{layer}.attention.output.dense.weight\").clone()\n    for h, f in scales.items(): W[:, h*32:(h+1)*32] *= f\n    return W\nWt = head_scale_edit(5, {0: 2.0, 6: 2.0}); print(\"changed entries for 2 heads:\", int((Wt != Wao).sum()))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3338,"cache_read_input_tokens":66886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3338},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabc22c4-c493-4939-8aac-1a1cdf219a55","uuid":"d637f75b-20f0-4330-aa7d-beaa93c45686","timestamp":"2026-11-13T14:17:09.003Z","request_id":"req_011Ch14yfYxkUQT8JuVm2FjP"}
